The attached Figure 6 illustrates that Nano-11, a dendrimer-like alpha-D-glucan nanoparticle, effectively activates dendritic cells (DCs) by enhancing the expression of crucial costimulatory molecules. Flow cytometry histograms show that compared to medium control (gray line), incubation with Nano-11 (black line) for two days resulted in a slight increase in CD40 expression and a marked, significant upregulation of both CD80 and CD86 on the DCs. This induction of costimulatory molecules signifies DC activation, which is essential for initiating an effective adaptive immune response, thus underscoring Nano-11's potential as a potent vaccine adjuvant.